{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607072300-actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index"
  :title "ADR-2607072300: actor public data git-repo residency -- git journal as source of truth, kotobase.net as derived index, DataLad opt-in for large binaries only"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-07"
  :authoritative_for
  ["An actor repo's own git history (a committed EDN quad-log under
    80-data/public/*.journal.edn) is the authoritative source of an actor's
    PUBLIC data -- not kotobase.net"
   "kotobase.net/kotobase-peer is a derived, rebuildable read index over
    that git-resident journal, not the sole store, for any actor that
    adopts this pattern"
   "DataLad (git-annex + B2) remains scoped to large-binary payloads a
    journal references by CID, extending the existing m365-archive/
    mangaka-data pattern per-actor on an opt-in basis -- not a general
    replication layer for structured public data"
   "kotoba-rad's role is unchanged from ADR-2607072200 (identity/
    authorization only): it signs and gates the journal's commits/refs once
    an actor repo runs on real kotoba-git history, but this ADR does not
    expand kotoba-rad into a data store"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607072200-kotoba-git-kotoba-rad-content-addressed-vcs.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607032430-kotoba-datom-log-structured-engine-redesign.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607022300-itonami-gftdcojp-private-tenant-kotoba-rad-git-storage.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607051410-net-kotobase-distributed-storage-mesh-design.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2606282000-cloud-workers-kotobase-external-storage.md"
   "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2606231200-kotoba-rad-sovereign-actor-identity.md"
   "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2606251200-kotoba-rad-git-transport-binding.md"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "Session question: for etzhayyim (and similar) actors, is there a
           design where PUBLIC data lives in the git repo itself, DataLad
           replicates large data, Radicle plays some role, and kotobase can
           query it? Owner instruction after research: \"do it\" (write the
           unifying ADR)."
  :facts
  ["Actor git repos (e.g. orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-cargo) hold only
    actor-manifest.jsonld (config incl. graph.query step DEFINITIONS) and
    .well-known/did.json -- zero literal business-data files committed."
   "An actor's actual data (\"the graph\") lives only in kotobase-peer/
    kotobase.net, reachable only via transact/q/pull/datoms XRPC -- git
    clone/west update + file read cannot reach it."
   "kotoba-rad (ADR-2607072200) is RID/delegate/sigref/push-gate only; no
    replication/gossip (kotoba-rad/README.md, explicit)."
   "DataLad (manifest/repos.edn :datalad) covers exactly two datasets --
    m365-archive, mangaka-data -- both large-binary archives, unrelated to
    actor public data."
   "The only git-resident, server-free public data today is
    orgs/etzhayyim/root/80-data/kotoba-rad/*.identity.journal.edn (320
    files, EDN quad-log [cid attr value tx op], verified on disk) -- but
    scoped to identity facts only, not business data."
   "ADR-2607032430 (D2) already targets 'actor = shard = repo = RID = graph
    = IPNS head' convergence; ADR-2607072200 already built the kotoba-git/
    kotoba-rad primitives on kotobase-peer -- but neither decided WHERE/HOW
    an actor's actual public data should be placed to realize that
    convergence."]}

 :decision
 {:summary "An actor's public data is authored as an EDN quad-log
            (80-data/public/*.journal.edn) committed directly into the
            actor's own repo -- the source of truth. kotobase.net/
            kotobase-peer becomes a derived, rebuildable index folded from
            that journal. DataLad stays scoped to large binaries the
            journal references by CID. kotoba-rad's role is unchanged from
            ADR-2607072200."
  :layering
  ["actor repo (GitHub, same transport as today) ->
    80-data/public/*.journal.edn: source of truth, EDN-reader-readable via
    plain git clone/west update, no server required"
   "Tier 1 (usable today, no new infra): journal file format identical to
    the existing identity journal's EDN quad vectors
    [\"<subject-cid-or-id>\" :attr value tx :add]; GitHub remains transport;
    does not wait for kotoba-git/kotoba-rad production wiring"
   "Tier 2 (future, after ADR-2607072200's own flagged transport/p2p
    follow-up lands): once an actor repo's canonical VCS host is kotoba-git
    itself, kotoba-git.repo/persist!'s arrangement quads ARE this journal;
    the flat EDN file becomes a derived artifact, not the source; kotoba-rad
    sigref/push-gate applies unchanged (it only ever handles plain CID
    strings) -- no new kotoba-rad code needed"
   "kotobase-peer ingestion (fold job, NOT implemented in this ADR): reads
    the journal and folds it into arrangement, so kotobase.net's XRPC
    graph.query surface (already assumed by actor-manifest.jsonld) serves
    low-latency indexed queries -- but the index is rebuildable from the
    journal, reversing today's 'kotobase.net is the only store' posture,
    and providing one mitigation to the single-point-of-failure posture
    flagged in ADR-2607051410"
   "DataLad (git-annex + B2, opt-in per-actor): only for large binaries a
    journal references by CID (images/video/model weights); journal stores
    the CID reference only, never the bytes -- mirrors kotoba-git's own
    'log holds content hash, bytes live elsewhere' shape; registered in
    manifest/repos.edn :datalad exactly like m365-archive/mangaka-data"
   "kotoba-rad role unchanged from ADR-2607072200: identity/authorization
    only, no data-store or replication responsibilities added"]
  :not-decided
  ["No ingestion pipeline (journal -> kotobase-peer fold job) code written
    here -- trigger mechanism (west update hook, GitHub webhook, kotobase.net
    pull) left undecided, design only."
   "No migration of the existing 320 identity journals, nor of any actor's
    existing kotobase business data, into this 80-data/public/ format --
    same 'follow-up, not done here' status ADR-2607072200 already gave this
    class of migration."
   "No pilot actor selected -- which actor first adopts
    80-data/public/*.journal.edn is an implementation-time decision."
   "No new conflict-resolution/merge convention for concurrent journal
    commits across parallel agent sessions -- relies on CLAUDE.md's existing
    worktree-per-agent + server-side-merge conventions, not re-derived here."
   "kotoba-git/kotoba-rad's own not-wired-to-production status is unchanged
    -- Tier 2 still waits on ADR-2607072200's own flagged p2p/transport
    patch; this ADR does not pull that forward."
   "No per-domain attribute vocabulary (e.g. :cargo/*, :gtin/*) decided for
    80-data/public/ journals -- left to each actor's own implementation."]}

 :consequences
 ["Any actor can today commit 80-data/public/*.journal.edn and get
   git-clone-readable public data immediately -- but without the (not yet
   built) ingestion job, it stays 'git-readable, not yet kotobase-queryable'.
   Closing that gap is the concrete next implementation step this ADR
   defines the shape for."
  "Gives ADR-2607032430's D2 convergence target ('actor = shard = repo = RID
   = graph = IPNS head') the concrete file-placement/schema decision it was
   missing."
  "Reframes kotobase.net from sole store to derived index over a
   git-authoritative source -- a scope shift relevant to ADR-2607051410's
   future distributed-storage-mesh work; recorded here as a cross-reference,
   not a rewrite of that ADR."
  "DataLad's scope stays large-binary-only/opt-in, explicitly NOT extended
   to general public-data replication in this ADR -- any future proposal to
   widen it should account for this decision."]

 :verification
 ["Zero implementation (design only). Grounded in on-disk verification of
   the existing identity journal file format, kotobase-peer's
   transact/q/pull API shape, and manifest/repos.edn's :datalad section
   format -- but no actor has written an 80-data/public/*.journal.edn file
   yet, and no ingestion job exists."]}
